Verify:

- Private signing key is never shipped to Android.
- Public verification key matches the actual publisher.
- Signature verification works.
- Asset SHA-256 hashes are checked.
- Modified bundles are rejected.
- Old or replayed releases cannot bypass version policy.
- Last-known-good UI remains available.

The publisher private key must use persistent, owner-controlled secure storage.

Do not store the only release-signing key in an ephemeral runtime filesystem.

Do not expose it through publisher JavaScript or public APIs.

## 8.3 WebSocket authentication

Check:

- Authenticated initial connection.
- Token verification.
- Device identity binding.
- Approved session checks.
- Sender and recipient checks.
- Command scope.
- Replay protection.
- Rate limiting.
- Secure session termination.

Do not trust client-supplied identity headers.

## 8.4 Sensitive command routing

Verify that:

- INPUT_EVENT.
- FILE_COMMAND.
- APP_COMMAND.
- DIAGNOSTICS_RUN.
- EMERGENCY_DISCONNECT.
- SDP and ICE messages.

are routed only to their authorized session participants.

No unauthorized broadcast must be possible.

## 8.5 TURN security

